    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">In the 1960s, U.S. President John F. Kennedy set forth the vision of landing a man on the moon—not only to send astronauts there but also to bring them safely back to Earth. Pfizer’s development of the COVID-19 vaccine was much like this moonshot mission. CEO Albert Bourla set what seemed like an impossible goal and led the pharmaceutical giant to partner with BioNTech. Together, they successfully created, tested, and manufactured the first mRNA vaccine in just nine months—a process that would normally take several years.</marc:subfield>
